{"parentUuid":"fb810e8d-6889-4e46-9790-0990faf44d14","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"20a0d440-52e4-4832-9421-52882cd9367b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FzGgNhxbczHUmwnLhuu5d5","type":"tool_result","content":"# Prime-Silo Project Summary\n\n## What It Does\nPrime-Silo is an open-source execution platform designed for institutional reasoning and decision-making. It combines a deterministic computational substrate with an adaptive browser-based interface, enabling operators to work with documents, code, and tabular data while maintaining full auditability and cryptographic signing.\n\n## Architecture Overview\nThe project merges two foundational systems:\n- **Benny** (vendored under `runtime/`): A deterministic substrate handling transformation algebra, cognitive operations, governance, and manifest signing\n- **Space-Agent**: A browser-resident shell providing adaptive interfaces and Git-backed workspace versioning\n\nA critical architectural principle separates operations into two zones: a deterministic zone (manifest authoring, execution, graph mutations) with read-only agent authority requiring human approval before signing, and a review zone (post-run analysis, audit queries) where agents can write to sandboxed directories.\n\n## Tech Stack\n- **Frontend**: JavaScript (65.1%), React components, WebGL for 3D visualization\n- **Backend**: Python (20.2%), FastAPI\n- **Additional**: TypeScript (8.4%), HTML, CSS, PowerShell\n\n## Main Features\n- Deterministic run execution with cryptographic lineage guarantees\n- Multi-surface unified cockpit (\"Bridge\") consolidating memory, documents, code, and execution flows\n- Knowledge graph ingestion from documents\n- Code graph visualization (2D/3D modes)\n- Session checkpointing with save/restore/fork capabilities\n- Memory graph integration (Memo-Ray) for session history tracking\n- Agent sandbox with fine-grained permission boundaries\n- Desktop and CLI interfaces\n\n## Claude/Anthropic Integration\nThe README explicitly identifies this as \"a Claude agent, built on Anthropic's Claude Agent SDK.\" Agents operate within defined permission boundaries, access system state via documented endpoints, and can read/write only to sandboxed directories. Integration patterns are detailed in `AGENT-AWARENESS.md` and `AGENTS.md`.\n\n## Repository Structure\n\n| Directory | Purpose |\n|-----------|---------|\n| `app/` | Space-Agent browser frontend |\n| `server/` | Node.js shell server |\n| `space/` | Agent runtime |\n| `packaging/` | Desktop builds |\n| `runtime/` | Vendored Benny backend and tests |\n| `scripts/` | Development/launch utilities |\n| `docs/`, `architecture/` | Configuration wizard and ADRs |\n| `manifests/integrations/` | Signed integration declarations |\n\n**Key files**: `QUICKSTART-EXE.md` (desktop setup), `CLI.md` (command reference), `OPERATING_MANUAL.md` (developer guide), `ADR-001` (design decisions)."}]},"uuid":"867e29dc-4d8a-4823-85ab-640184e69326","timestamp":"2026-06-25T09:21:24.251Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":415222,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Prime-Silo Project Summary\n\n## What It Does\nPrime-Silo is an open-source execution platform designed for institutional reasoning and decision-making. It combines a deterministic computational substrate with an adaptive browser-based interface, enabling operators to work with documents, code, and tabular data while maintaining full auditability and cryptographic signing.\n\n## Architecture Overview\nThe project merges two foundational systems:\n- **Benny** (vendored under `runtime/`): A deterministic substrate handling transformation algebra, cognitive operations, governance, and manifest signing\n- **Space-Agent**: A browser-resident shell providing adaptive interfaces and Git-backed workspace versioning\n\nA critical architectural principle separates operations into two zones: a deterministic zone (manifest authoring, execution, graph mutations) with read-only agent authority requiring human approval before signing, and a review zone (post-run analysis, audit queries) where agents can write to sandboxed directories.\n\n## Tech Stack\n- **Frontend**: JavaScript (65.1%), React components, WebGL for 3D visualization\n- **Backend**: Python (20.2%), FastAPI\n- **Additional**: TypeScript (8.4%), HTML, CSS, PowerShell\n\n## Main Features\n- Deterministic run execution with cryptographic lineage guarantees\n- Multi-surface unified cockpit (\"Bridge\") consolidating memory, documents, code, and execution flows\n- Knowledge graph ingestion from documents\n- Code graph visualization (2D/3D modes)\n- Session checkpointing with save/restore/fork capabilities\n- Memory graph integration (Memo-Ray) for session history tracking\n- Agent sandbox with fine-grained permission boundaries\n- Desktop and CLI interfaces\n\n## Claude/Anthropic Integration\nThe README explicitly identifies this as \"a Claude agent, built on Anthropic's Claude Agent SDK.\" Agents operate within defined permission boundaries, access system state via documented endpoints, and can read/write only to sandboxed directories. Integration patterns are detailed in `AGENT-AWARENESS.md` and `AGENTS.md`.\n\n## Repository Structure\n\n| Directory | Purpose |\n|-----------|---------|\n| `app/` | Space-Agent browser frontend |\n| `server/` | Node.js shell server |\n| `space/` | Agent runtime |\n| `packaging/` | Desktop builds |\n| `runtime/` | Vendored Benny backend and tests |\n| `scripts/` | Development/launch utilities |\n| `docs/`, `architecture/` | Configuration wizard and ADRs |\n| `manifests/integrations/` | Signed integration declarations |\n\n**Key files**: `QUICKSTART-EXE.md` (desktop setup), `CLI.md` (command reference), `OPERATING_MANUAL.md` (developer guide), `ADR-001` (design decisions).","durationMs":20950,"url":"https://github.com/binary16labs/prime-silo"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fb810e8d-6889-4e46-9790-0990faf44d14","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","c