{"parentUuid":"97c62062-ac80-4206-835b-917d6cc54f3a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"20a0d440-52e4-4832-9421-52882cd9367b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KGWk98xqSv9L6pZQMciXhH","type":"tool_result","content":"# Memo-Ray Page Analysis\n\n## Core Purpose\nMemo-Ray is an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server designed to preserve context and extract skills across long-running agent workflows, addressing the problem of token expiration during extended development sessions.\n\n## Main Claims About Token Savings\nThe page asserts that Memo-Ray eliminates the \"Token Tax\"—the cost of re-ingesting raw historical logs when sessions expire. It claims the approach avoids \"$O(N^2) raw file tokens\" by locally parsing data and feeding agents \"highly condensed, pre-calculated summaries\" instead of raw JSON and logs.\n\n## Tests, Benchmarks, and Numbers Shown\nThe page displays comparative visualizations but **provides no actual numerical data**. Six token audit scenarios are presented with placeholder sections for:\n- Direct file access token counts\n- MCP resolution token counts\n- Raw payload comparisons\n\nThese appear to be template structures awaiting populated data rather than completed benchmarks.\n\n## Page Sections & Navigation\n- Genesis (problem statement)\n- Token Audit (6 comparison scenarios)\n- Session Graphs (interactive visualizations)\n- Skill Extraction (pattern analysis)\n- Setup Wizard (installation guide with platform selection)\n\n**No review sub-pages or external links to case studies are present.**\n\n## Relation to Claude/Anthropic\nMemo-Ray explicitly targets \"Anthropic Claude\" as a primary integration point and references \"Anthropic-Style Design Pivot\" in the footer. It leverages Claude's official MCP configuration system for deployment."}]},"uuid":"4d494d11-8f29-4a8c-b513-e319ad5d3729","timestamp":"2026-06-25T09:21:40.712Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":65047,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Memo-Ray Page Analysis\n\n## Core Purpose\nMemo-Ray is an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server designed to preserve context and extract skills across long-running agent workflows, addressing the problem of token expiration during extended development sessions.\n\n## Main Claims About Token Savings\nThe page asserts that Memo-Ray eliminates the \"Token Tax\"—the cost of re-ingesting raw historical logs when sessions expire. It claims the approach avoids \"$O(N^2) raw file tokens\" by locally parsing data and feeding agents \"highly condensed, pre-calculated summaries\" instead of raw JSON and logs.\n\n## Tests, Benchmarks, and Numbers Shown\nThe page displays comparative visualizations but **provides no actual numerical data**. Six token audit scenarios are presented with placeholder sections for:\n- Direct file access token counts\n- MCP resolution token counts\n- Raw payload comparisons\n\nThese appear to be template structures awaiting populated data rather than completed benchmarks.\n\n## Page Sections & Navigation\n- Genesis (problem statement)\n- Token Audit (6 comparison scenarios)\n- Session Graphs (interactive visualizations)\n- Skill Extraction (pattern analysis)\n- Setup Wizard (installation guide with platform selection)\n\n**No review sub-pages or external links to case studies are present.**\n\n## Relation to Claude/Anthropic\nMemo-Ray explicitly targets \"Anthropic Claude\" as a primary integration point and references \"Anthropic-Style Design Pivot\" in the footer. It leverages Claude's official MCP configuration system for deployment.","durationMs":7700,"url":"https://binary16labs.github.io/memo-ray/"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"97c62062-ac80-4206-835b-917d6cc54f3a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"101cdbf9-13c9-4450-a0b5-a384b75b301d","version":"2.1.181","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"ce1b21b2-7f83-41dc-9dfa-0267e0c9f02b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"20a0d440-52e4-4832-9421-52882cd9367b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y5KQuQMHEuQd2NqMfHv1m5","type":"tool_result","content":"# Memo-Ray Repository Summary\n\n## What It Does\nMemo-Ray is a visualization tool that reads AI agent session logs (from Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Cowork, and Antigravity) and transforms them into an interactive, searchable lineage graph. It presents prompts, tool calls, file interactions, and artifacts as an explorable spatial interface rather than dense JSON logs.\n\n## Token Savings & Benchmarks\nThe page contains **no token savings claims or benchmark data**. The tool focuses on memory management and cognitive organization rather than token efficiency.\n\n## Core Principle\nThe developers frame it as solving an institutional memory problem: \"Operators end up acting as the _glue_ between their agents — remembering which session touched which file, why a decision was made.\" Memo-Ray aims to externalize this burden into a queryable graph layer.\n\n## Tech Stack\n- **Frontend**: Vite + React (port 5175)\n- **Backend**: Express.js (port 3030)\n- **Languages**: JavaScript (56.9%), HTML (32.2%), CSS (9.5%), Python (1.1%)\n- **Data**: Atomic JSON file-system database with delta-sync indexing\n\n## Key Directories\n- `agent-os-dashboard/` — Main application\n- `mcp-server/` — MCP integration\n- `scripts/` — Dev launchers (PowerShell/Bash)\n- `server/data/` — Git-ignored session storage\n\n## Documentation\nNo dedicated review page or external docs site is referenced. Internal documentation includes `requirements/PRD.md` and `data_model_abstract.md`."}]},"uuid":"02179615-8e60-4358-b679-e938abc8e870","timestamp":"2026-06-25T09:21:49.751Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":297391,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Memo-Ray Repository Summary\n\n## What It Does\nMemo-Ray is a visualization tool that reads AI agent session log