\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 101cdbf9-13c9-4450-a0b5-a384b75b301d\n---\n\nReviewing Memo-Ray's \"Token Tax\" / token-save claim (the Token Audit section on the GitHub Pages site `dist/index.html`, data from `dist/mcp_benchmark_results.js`, generator `mcp-server/run_benchmark.js`). The `binary16labs.github.io/memo-ray/review` deep-link 404s — the published site is a single `index.html` at root with no `/review` route.\n\n**Verdict (2026-06-25):** the underlying MCP design is sound (tools do real server-side aggregation via `DataReader`, returning condensed summaries — the correct off-context pattern), but the v1 benchmark does NOT validate the claim. Defects in `run_benchmark.js`: (1) tokens = `Math.ceil(str.length/4)`, not a real tokenizer; (2) no model call — output tokens hardcoded; (3) model labelled \"Gemini 3.5 Flash\" but cost constants are Claude Sonnet pricing ($3/$15 per M); (4) injected additive constants on the no-MCP arm (+500/+1500/+2000/+3000/+4000) vs +100 on MCP — these manufacture the savings; (5) strawman baseline (always recursive full-tree disk load); (6) Test 2 (full timeline) honestly shows MCP slightly WORSE (101515 vs 102066), hidden in the ~51% aggregate; N=1.\n\n**What I built:** `mcp-server/run_benchmark_v2.js` — counts both arms' real payloads with Anthropic `count_tokens` (`POST /v1/messages/count_tokens`, exact, free, model=`claude-opus-4-8` by default), removes all injected constants, measures input/context tokens only (output explicitly out of scope, no model call), runs multi-target, and flags each scenario `fair` vs `worst-case` — the headline excludes strawman baselines so it can't be inflated. Outputs `dist/token_audit_v2.json`.\n\n**Dual-mode (subscriber-friendly):** `mcp-server/tokenizer.js` `makeCounter()` — offline by default via `@anthropic-ai/tokenizer` (real legacy Claude BPE, NO key, zero spend, runs against live local data) and exact `count_tokens` API when `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set (`TOKENIZER=offline|api` forces). Both `@anthropic-ai/sdk` and `@anthropic-ai/tokenizer` installed in `mcp-server/`.\n\n**Validated (offline, 2026-06-25)** → `dist/token_audit_v2.json`. Headline (FAIR scenarios only, strawman excluded): **40.6% input-token reduction** (149,818→88,962). Per scenario: Get Latest Session 90.0%, Sliding Window 75.8%, Reconstruct Full Timeline **3.4% (control — MCP barely helps when you genuinely need all history; v1 hid this)**, Query-by-Project 94.0% but flagged worst-case/strawman and excluded. Conclusion: claim holds DIRECTIONALLY and is large for summary-shaped queries, ~0 for full-history. Re-run with key for exact numbers. NB: data-reader.js:216 also uses length/4 for its graph token estimates. Next: Phase 2 `/review` page rendering this JSON. Frontend :5175, backend :3030. Related: [[project_binary16_app_registry]], [[benny_pilot_documents_and_no_selection_fix]].\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":15,"oldLines":4,"newStart":15,"newLines":6,"lines":[" "," **Dual-mode (subscriber-friendly):** `mcp-server/tokenizer.js` `makeCounter()` — offline by default via `@anthropic-ai/tokenizer` (real legacy Claude BPE, NO key, zero spend, runs against live local data) and exact `count_tokens` API when `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set (`TOKENIZER=offline|api` forces). Both `@anthropic-ai/sdk` and `@anthropic-ai/tokenizer` installed in `mcp-server/`."," ","-**Validated (offline, 2026-06-25)** → `dist/token_audit_v2.json`. Headline (FAIR scenarios only, strawman excluded): **40.6% input-token reduction** (149,818→88,962). Per scenario: Get Latest Session 90.0%, Sliding Window 75.8%, Reconstruct Full Timeline **3.4% (control — MCP barely helps when you genuinely need all history; v1 hid this)**, Query-by-Project 94.0% but flagged worst-case/strawman and excluded. Conclusion: claim holds DIRECTIONALLY and is large for summary-shaped queries, ~0 for full-history. Re-run with key for exact numbers. NB: data-reader.js:216 also uses length/4 for its grap